The trail features around 90 permanent shelters at designated campsites. The trail is also part of the 6,000 kilometres (3,700 mi) long North Sea Trail, which passes through Sweden, Norway, Denmark, Germany, the Netherlands and the United Kingdom. It connects to the neighbouring trails of Blekingeleden to the east, sharing some sections with it and Hallandsleden to the north, meeting at Koarp in Hallandsåsen.

